{
  "_comment": [
    "THE registry of every public number or policy value, tied to the code or config that makes it true (#1722).",
    "",
    "Checked by scripts/check-facts.mjs, by hand before a release that affects every app (the pre-release-sweeps",
    "skill): the repo, then the DEPLOYED website (--deployed). Not in CI. Values like these change rarely, and when one does nobody",
    "greps the website for it: /learn said 'two kinds of loss' for weeks after #720 made it three.",
    "",
    "Each fact:",
    "  value_from  {file, pattern} (or a list of them, which must all agree, e.g. a code default and the prod",
    "              wrangler var): the first capture group is the value. Arithmetic (15 * 60) and number words",
    "              (three) are evaluated; divide / multiply convert units; map renames a string; type: string",
    "              keeps it verbatim; measure: length counts the capture's characters, count: <regex> its matches. Prod config",
    "              (pollis-delivery/wrangler.prod.jsonc) is the public truth.",
    "  unit        for messages only.",
    "  words       false when the value must not be written as a word (ML-KEM-768 is never 'seven hundred').",
    "  asserted_in [{file, pattern, status?, note?}]: every place we state it. {value} expands to the value in",
    "              every form (12, twelve, Twelve; 10000, 10,000). Patterns match the text with HTML tags and",
    "              entities removed, Markdown ** removed, and all whitespace collapsed to one space.",
    "  status      ok (default) | disputed. Disputed problems are warnings that print both values and never fail.",
    "              It is for a legal or policy page that disagrees with code (#1720 'Policy vs code'): neither",
    "              side is automatically right, so the owner decides. Set it on one assertion, not the fact,",
    "              when only that copy disagrees.",
    "",
    "An assertion fails when its pattern states a different value (stale copy) and when it is not found at all",
    "(the text moved or was reworded, so the fact is no longer anchored). Rewording public copy therefore means",
    "re-anchoring its pattern here, in the same PR."
  ],
  "facts": {
